            </a>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Size the deck to your stride, and your
            stride is set by pace before height.</strong> Walkers are well served
            at 50 by 18. Joggers want 55 by 20. Anyone running, or anyone over
            5 foot 10, should treat 60 by 20 as the floor rather than the
            upgrade.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed">
            Pair the deck decision with the
            <a href="/treadmill-horsepower-guide/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">motor sizing guide</a>,
            because a large belt on a small motor is worse than either problem
            alone, and check the machine physically fits using
            <a href="/treadmill-dimensions-space-requirements/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">dimensions and space requirements</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
